            <div xml:id="d568">

                <pb facs="0633" n="529" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg529"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01 Manchuria/25: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-03-08T11:00:00+08:00">March 8, 1932—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 8—1:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>312. 1. Following from the American Consul at Harbin: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>[“] March 7, noon. Local Commissioner for Foreign Affairs has invited me
                            to attend congratulatory celebration formation new government March 9th.
                            Please advise what action I should take.”</p></quote></p>
                <p>2. Legation has replied that, as indicated in the Department’s March 3, 10 a.m.,
                    Consul should take no action in this matter or others of a similar character in
                    the absence of the Department’s specific instructions. It is suggested that the
                    Department reply direct to Harbin.</p>
                <p>3. Following from American Consul General at Mukden: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“March 7, 3 p.m. I have received an official invitation from the
                            Northeastern Administration Commission to attend the inauguration of the
                            executive at Changchun on March 9, 3 p.m. This is the first
                            communication received from new regime. I have no intention of attending
                            nor do I consider it advisable to send an unofficial observer from this
                            office.”</p></quote></p>
                <p>Foregoing is being repeated to American Consul at Harbin for his information.</p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Perkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
